rota lap 4179, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in; the threshold says take the concrete fact off the face before arguing with it, and the fact on the face of my own cold open was stash_record red at unlanded=1 naming one path.
think Opened with the cold roster and held still through it -- 39 minutes, one red: stash_record, evidence at construction/standing-equipment-reds/stash_record.txt.
think Read the evidence rather than the count. stashes=12 records=12 landed=11 unlanded=1 orphans=21. sh tools/fixtures/s/stash_record_scan.sh list names the one gated path on its own line: session-logs/date/20260907/20260907-111425_the-fence-the-neighbour-had.kyri.
think git stash show --stat stash@{0} then read that log out of the stash. A whole lap of this lane -- mantra/src/diff.rye +153, diff_witness.rye +114, the control and the witness -- finished, GREEN by its own record, and never committed.
think The previous Patchouli lap SAW this red and wrote "two reds stand that are not this lap's and not this lane's: stash_record reads 21 orphaned round-open stashes". The 21 orphans are honest -- files a peer's landed work already carries. The gated reading is unlanded, it read 1, and its one path names this lane.
think So reds-first chose the lap: recover and land, rather than open anything new.
obs The number had to move and the stamp did not. The parked row booked %561; git fetch xy showed %561 published to a peer's door-has-two-keys row within the parked hours, and reds_spine_derive --next answered 570. (This log was itself parked before it could ship, and a peer published %570 in the meantime, so the same renumbering ran a second time to %572 -- the stamp still never moved.) Card, recital, shelf filename and the log's own two citations moved; the row's identity, 20260907.111135, never did. That is derived-spine working exactly as written, and it cost one file rather than a sweep because the parked lap had cited by stamp.
obs Two duplicates refused rather than landed. The stash carried construction/archive/20260907-111135_itinerary-landed-accounts.md holding the %560 account -- which a peer had already shelved at 20260907-120258 while the work sat parked -- so the duplicate shelf was deleted, %512's two-shelf fault caught before shipping. And the stash's index row for the recovered log prepended to the top of the day shelf, where in stamp order it belongs between 111550 and 111425's true neighbours; moved rather than left, since %440 is exactly that row out of order.
obs What the recovered lap proved stands unchanged and re-run rather than trusted: mantra_diff_witness GREEN on metal, ten control phases, tame_style_check GREEN, width-check ok at its ceilings.
obs The card would not hold the account at its first two lengths -- 42,260 then 41,743 against a bound of 40,960, upstream having closed at 40,935 with 25 bytes free. Condensed to 40,939 by moving the diff finding's detail onto the REDS shelf it already has, one click away, rather than by touching a peer's block.
obs Not taken, named: the several-line interleave is Keaton's word; store.rye's inline 1024 * 1024 read buffer and main.rye's private split_lines are the next two unnamed ceilings in this lane, both agent-doable.
obs One repair outside my own block, named: the card's INCENSE line cited archive/REDS-the-door-has-two-keys-rows-565.md where that row folded to rows-561 -- caught by the QA card's own Truth reading as unresolved, and repointed rather than left, since a reference is a promise and the same renumbering churn wrote it.
obs Two more reds on the hot pass, both closed here. unshared_citation red at 1: my card cited the number the spine had yet to bind, which is derived-spine rule 4 in the direction the law was written for -- the card and the shelf row cite the stamp now, and the archives are exempt by definition. reds_pin_capacity red at unrecorded_shelves=63 against a ceiling of 62, and it reads 63 at HEAD too, so it was a peer's: REDS-the-meter-that-read-one-of-two-instruments-rows-566.md landed at 12:40 with no line in the fold recital. A trail that ends mid-sentence is closable by any hand, so the line was added and the reading is 62 again.
obs My own slip, named: I ran git stash --keep-index to measure HEAD's unrecorded count, and the pop conflicted the card against its own staged copy. Nothing was lost -- both sides were mine, minutes apart -- and it is recorded because the cheap way to ask what HEAD holds is git show and git ls-tree, which read the commit without moving the tree at all.
